  <section>
    <h2 id="entry-rules">Do International Visitors Need a Visa?</h2>
    <p><strong>Your nationality, travel document, trip purpose and route determine the answer.</strong> Check whether a current bilateral or unilateral visa-exemption policy covers your visit. If it does, use that policy’s own duration and conditions. Otherwise, assess transit eligibility or arrange the appropriate visa before departure.</p>
    <p>For a business-focused fair visit requiring a visa, ask the Chinese embassy, consulate or visa center serving your place of residence which category and supporting documents apply. Do not treat a visitor badge or invitation letter as permission to enter China.</p>

    <h3>Can You Attend Using 240-Hour Visa-Free Transit?</h3>
    <p>Potentially. NIA’s <a href="https://en.nia.gov.cn/n147418/n147468/c217849/content.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">August 20, 2026 announcement</a> confirms <strong>57 eligible nationalities and 65 ports</strong>. Short business visits are allowed; work, study and news reporting require the relevant prior approvals and visas.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Hold an ordinary passport from an eligible country, with at least three months’ validity, and meet your onward destination’s entry requirements.</li>
      <li>Travel through Mainland China to a different country or region, with onward tickets showing a confirmed seat and departure date.</li>
      <li>Enter through an eligible port, remain within permitted areas and leave within the authorized period.</li>
      <li>Apply for temporary entry at immigration inspection and cooperate with document checks.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Read NIA’s <a href="https://en.nia.gov.cn/n147418/n147463/c183412/content.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">current transit policy</a> and <a href="https://en.nia.gov.cn/n147418/n147468/c187308/content.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">published document and timing requirements</a>. For the full arrival process, see our <a href="/china-240-hour-visa-free-transit/">China 240-hour visa-free transit guide</a>.</p>

    <h3>Practical Route Examples</h3>
    <p>Compare the country or region <strong>immediately before</strong> Mainland China with the one <strong>immediately after</strong> it. These examples test routing only; they do not guarantee entry.</p>
